=== diff on in-scope view files ===
commit 66f0a5adc7b6a9a6224872de242ed46aebc41e11
Author: Shabakebehdasht <Shabakebehdasht@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Sat Oct 17 08:36:40 2026 +0000

    fix(#1023): single-pass boundary GeoJSON projection on map screens
    
    Project ST_AsGeoJSON(boundaries.boundary) in the query on the unit-map
    readers instead of reading Boundary::$appends['geojson'] per row, which
    fired one boundary query per region/unit and round-tripped the geometry.
    
    - maps/unit: region, center and sub-type queries now join `boundaries` and
      select the bare geometry; scope/region/type filters are qualified to their
      table so the join is unambiguous.
    - units/map: load the single unit with a LEFT join (an inner join would make
      boundary-less units — the draw path — disappear) and read `geojson`.
    - Boundary: drop the dead `multipolygon` cast (the column is `boundary`);
      remove its now-unmatched baseline entry (deletion only, 0 additions).
    - Tests: query-count regressions for both screens, bare-MultiPolygon payload
      contract, boundary-less omission, fail-closed out-of-scope unit.

